      "message": "Changing the shims used to build a test depending on the branch is not something we have in other mainline-compatible tests, the general approach we have is to completely disable the targets that don\u0027t make sense in sc-mainline-prod there.\n\nSo instead of switching with network_stack_shims, could you duplicate the android_test_helper_app to have CtsHostsideNetworkTestsApp (based on stable shims) and CtsHostsideNetworkTestsAppNext (based on current shims), and have CtsHostsideNetworkTestsAppNext use ConnectivityNextEnableDefaults ? This would disable the CtsHostsideNetworkTestsAppNext build rule in sc-mainline-prod (using the \"standard\" default we have for that).\n\nThen in com.android.cts.net.HostsideNetworkTestCase, use com.android.modules.utils.build.testing.DeviceSdkLevel to install CtsHostsideNetworkTestsAppNext if the device is T+, and CtsHostsideNetworkTestsApp if it is older.\n\nQuick notes we had in a meeting discussing this: go/conn-hostside-multi-sdk-cts-testing",
